The clean LLVM semantics build succeeded, and 20 fresh `krun` executions—covering both concrete-list strings and the claim’s `segment/seed` representation—matched both Python implementations on normal, empty, unequal-length, and branch-boundary inputs. The Haskell proof definition also rebuilt, and the complete submitted spec plus the isolated helper claim each printed `#Top`. I’m checking the end-to-end claim’s dependency on the helper claim rather than treating an unbounded isolated unroll as a proof failure.
